I hope not, but yes, that's what the definition of {lo'e}
suggests. I would use {le cnano be le ka plini} for that.

It doesn't seem at all necessary to have a special grammar
category for the concept of average. On the other hand,
it is necessary to distinguish the seeking of planets
(independently of whether or not there are any to be
found) from the situation where there is a planet being
sought. So I just try to give some use to an otherwise
not very useful word.

